  "verbalization": "Mitomycin's relationship with SMMC-7721 is supported by multiple pathways, all of which involve the drug interacting through palmarumycin CP18 as a mediator. The evidence suggests that mitomycin targets multiple proteins, including Bromodomain-containing protein 4 and Ubiquitin carboxyl-terminal hydrolase 5, which are both targets of palmarumycin CP18. These proteins, in turn, interact with SMMC-7721, indicating a potential mechanism where mitomycin exerts its effects via palmarumycin CP18, which may modulate cellular processes in the SMMC-7721 cell line. The varying scores in the paths reflect the strength of the relationships, with the highest confidence in the connection through Bromodomain-containing protein 4. The integration of these pathways highlights the role of palmarumycin CP18 as a central mediator in the drug's interaction with SMMC-7721, suggesting a possible mechanism involving the regulation of cellular functions through these targets.",
